- Cap, to prevent spills and contamination;
- Handle, for ease of carrying;
- Spout, for controlled pouring;
- Material, typically metal or plastic;
- Capacity, varies depending on design;
- Weight, generally lightweight for ease of use;
- Closure mechanism, may include a latch or screw cap;
- Color, often bright to be easily visible;
- Surface finish, may be smooth or textured for grip;
- Branding, possible logos or labels for identification;
- Compatibility, designed to hold specific types of oil;
- Size, varies from small handheld to larger industrial types;
- Durability, typically made from materials that can withstand wear;
- Ergonomic design, for comfortable and efficient use;
- Safety features, like dripless spouts or non-slip bases;
- Recyclability, some cans are made from recyclable materials.
